.TH ZERODDS-CORBA-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-corba-bridged \- DDS to CORBA GIOP/IIOP bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-corba-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH=VALUE\fR]...
[\fB\-\-check\-config\fR]
[\fB\-\-iiop\-bind\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fIREPO_ID=TOPIC\fR]...
[\fB\-\-dump\-iors\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-corba-bridged
maps CORBA operations onto DDS request/reply topic pairs and DDS samples
onto oneway CORBA calls. It serves IIOP and, with a certificate, SSLIOP;
it writes one IOR per mapping. GIOP 1.0 to 1.2 are accepted; a mapped
operation needs GIOP 1.2.
With
.BR corba.csiv2.enabled ,
every request's SAS
.I EstablishContext
is evaluated against a GSSUP password file (CORBA 3.4 Part 2 \(sc10/\(sc24);
a rejected one gets
.B NO_PERMISSION
with a SAS
.B ContextError
attached, additively next to SSLIOP client certificates and the ACL.
With
.BR corba.ior.publish_to_naming ,
every mapping's IOR is
.B rebind
into
.B corba.ior.naming_service
(a
.IR corbaname: " or " corbaloc:
URL) at start and
.B unbind
at a clean stop.
.B corba.naming.serve
(hosting a NameService in-process, sharing this daemon's own transport) is
not built.
Implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-corba-bridge-1.0.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Base file, plus \fIFILE\fR.d/. Without it:
.I corba-bridged.yaml
and
.I corba-bridged.d/
in the system directory. See
.BR zerodds-corba-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-set =\fIPATH=VALUE\fR
One value above all files; repeatable. Every option below except
\fB\-\-dump\-iors\fR is short for \fB\-\-set\fR of its file key.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-config
Check the configuration, print every value with its origin, exit
0 (valid) or 1 (invalid).
.TP
.BR \-\-iiop\-bind =\fIADDR\fR
IIOP listen address. Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0:6833 .
.TP
.BR \-\-ssliop\-bind =\fIADDR\fR
SSLIOP listen address; enables SSLIOP. Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0:6834 .
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID.
.TP
.BR \-\-orb\-id =\fIID\fR
ORB-Identity.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
SSLIOP server certificate (PEM); only together with \fB\-\-tls\-key\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
SSLIOP server key (PEM).
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fIREPO_ID=TOPIC\fR
One more mapping, repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-\-dump\-iors
Print one line per mapping,
.IR "repo_id operation IOR:..." ,
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listen addr.
.PP
Test hooks. Real options, documented because the program accepts them
and an option nobody can find is one nobody maintains.
.TP
.BR \-\-idle\-timeout\-ms =\fIN\fR
Stop after \fIN\fR milliseconds, as on SIGTERM.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT stop the daemon: requests arriving then get
.BR TRANSIENT ,
pending requests get their reply or their
.B TIMEOUT
for at most 30 s, then every connection gets CloseConnection.
SIGHUP reads the configuration again: the ACL and the SSLIOP certificate
apply from then on (the certificate to new connections); changed mappings,
binds or domain need a restart and are logged. A configuration that does
not load changes nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318.
.TP
.B ZERODDS_CORBA_ADVERTISE_HOST
The host the IORs name when
.B corba.iiop.bind
is a wildcard address; the setting
.BR corba.iiop.advertise_host ,
above the files, below
.BR \-\-set .
Default
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 normal stop, 1 configuration, 2 bind, 3 DDS, 4 TLS.
.SH FILES
.IR /etc/zerodds/corba-bridged.yaml ,
the file named by
.BR corba.ior.ior_file .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-corba-bridged.yaml (5).
.SH STANDARDS
CORBA 3.3, GIOP 1.2, SSLIOP.
.SH AUTHORS
ZeroDDS Contributors.
